Status: DONE
Milestone: New frozen living-face edition with exact-definition navigation
Dependencies: vr-89, vr-90

Purpose:
  Owner wants every technical concept/new topic explained simply and cutely,
  with each occurrence clickable directly to its appendix definition.

Tasks:
  Inventory terminology across prose, captions, notes and historical registers.
  Author grouped plain-language explanations, analogies and precise limits.
  Add explicit appendix input to the existing portable journal builder.
  Link all recognized technical-word/phrase occurrences in PDF and offline HTML.
  Provide alphabetical lookup, exact definition anchors and native bookmarks.
  Test repeated/wrapped phrases, boundaries, longest matches and invalid inputs.
  Review complete new edition; preserve frozen v1 and prior volumes unchanged.

Acceptance criteria:
  Every inventoried concept has a real explanation, not an unexplained acronym.
  Matching is case-insensitive, whole-word and longest-phrase first.
  Links target the actual definition position, not merely the appendix start.
  Repeated prose/caption terms work in both PDF and offline HTML without scripts.
  All source text remains searchable/selectable and all links are local/valid.
  Complete native/reader/link qualification and portable frozen-input rebuild.
  No new images, runtime disturbance, source-cutoff rewrite or owner-approval claim.

